sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as Operator
    participant UI as Web UI
    participant SS as Secret Service
    participant Auto as Automation
    participant API as Control Plane
    participant EX as Executor
    participant AG as Agent Container

    Note over Op,SS: Operator manages secrets via Web UI. Secret Service is the only CRUD client.

    Op->>UI: Open Secrets page
    UI->>SS: POST /secrets { name, value, scope }
    SS->>SS: Encrypt, persist (audit logged)
    SS-->>UI: 201 secret_id
    UI-->>Op: Secret saved

    Note over Auto,EX: Task time. Control Plane knows only secret_ids, builds scope.

    Auto->>API: POST /tasks { prompt, tools, secret_ids: [a, b] }
    API->>API: Build scope = HMAC(project_id, task_id, secret_ids, TTL)
    API->>API: Persist task
    API-->>Auto: 202 task_id

    EX->>API: pick task
    API-->>EX: task_spec + scope_token

    EX->>EX: Pull image
    EX->>SS: POST /secrets/get-by-scope { scope_token }
    SS->>SS: Validate scope signature, expiry, project
    SS-->>EX: { "a": "...", "b": "..." }
    EX->>AG: Start container, mount secrets as env / tmpfs
    Note over AG: Has secrets from start. No runtime fetch needed unless refreshed.

    Note over AG,EX: On task end. Container terminated. Scope token expires. Plaintext gone.
